-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov 26 16:50:53 UTC 2026 - Jan Engelhardt <jengelh@inai.de>

- Update to release 1.5
  * The test suite no longer assumes an order of the conjugacy
    classes of a character table, or that `Irr` selects the method
    of this package. Both assumptions fail when the `CCTab` package
    is loaded.
  * Fixed `IrrUnger( G, opts )` and `CharacterTableUnger( G, opts
    )`, which returned wrong characters or raised an error when
    called a second time for the same group. Every call with
    options now runs the algorithm anew. `UngerRecord( G )` is now
    the finished record of the run with the default options.
  * Fixed `IrrUnger` and `CharacterTableUnger` with option
    `DoCyclicFirst`, which raised an error for the trivial group.
  * The manual states that `CharacterTableUnger( G )` stores its
    result in `G`, and its `InfoCTUnger` example no longer shows a
    trace for a stored result.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Aug  1 10:21:45 UTC 2026 - Jan Engelhardt <jengelh@inai.de>

- Update to release 1.4
  * Dropped the dependency on the `GAPDoc` package, which was only
    needed for building the manual.
  * The test suite no longer requires the `SmallGrp` package.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 17 11:46:24 UTC 2025 - Jan Engelhardt <jengelh@inai.de>

- Update to release 1.3
  * Set power maps in the character tables whose irreducibles have
    been computed by the `Irr` method that calls `IrrUnger`.
  * In the `Irr` method that calls `IrrUnger`, delegate to
    `IrrBaumClausen` if the group is abelian-by-supersolvable; this
    is usually faster.

